        "original_id": "c67d7ab5-0bc8-50c9-950b-e8d4e1a3896b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Big Sean, Chris Brown, Jhené Aiko, James Fauntleroy, Mike Posner, Kelly Rowland, Lil Wayne, Rick Ross, DJ Khaled\n- Groups: B2K, The Olympicks, Triple C's\n- Projects: Detroit, I Am Not a Human Being, Teflon Don, Custom Cars & Cycles, Kiss The Ring, Lay It on Me\n- Places: Detroit, Michigan\n- Topics: hip-hop music industry, music career, vocals, music videos\n\nFacts:\n- Jhené Aiko began her music career by contributing vocals and appearing in several music videos for the R&B group B2K.\n- The Olympicks originated in Detroit, Michigan.\n- The Olympicks have worked on hip-hop projects including Lil Wayne's \"I Am Not a Human Being,\" Rick Ross' \"Teflon Don,\" Triple C's \"Custom Cars & Cycles,\" DJ Khaled's \"Kiss The Ring,\" and Big Sean's mixtape \"Detroit.\"\n- Big Sean's mixtape \"Detroit\" includes appearances by American singers Chris Brown, Jhené Aiko, James Fauntleroy, and Mike Posner.\n- \"Lay It on Me\" is a song by Kelly Rowland that features two rap verses from Big Sean.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
